From 07b0913999003a7cf1b32bb7656065cb86eb327e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 01:04:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(post): write an inverted machine axis mirrored - sign,
 I/J/K, G2/G3, G41/G42

The engine mirrors the record stream once (post::invert) for a machine
whose X and/or Y is inverted. Coordinates, arc centres, the Start chain
and the work-offset origin on that axis negate, and the stock box edges
swap. An arc in a plane holding exactly one inverted axis reverses (G2 <->
G3). XY cutter compensation swaps sides (G41 <-> G42) when exactly one of
X and Y is inverted. A standard machine's records are untouched.

Refused by name, nothing posted: an inverted Z or any other letter, a
script without axisInversion = true (only Fanuc and Haas declare it),
helical arcs, threading cycles, tilted A/B/C moves, C-axis live tooling,
probing, an unpaired stock edge, and a static axis stating reversal.

Pinned by inverted-X Fanuc/Haas goldens and by a controller-
interpretation equivalence test (inverted X, Y and X+Y): the posted
program read by the inverted controller follows the CAM path within
0.002 mm, and the untranslated program does not.

Fixes #374

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
